WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book four.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.990
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:15.414
Unit thirteen: Brand Management. Today you will describe brand stability with consistency language.

4
00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.494
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:22.597
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.602
Brand identity.

7
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:31.076
Brand identity means the visible elements and values a company uses to present itself.

8
00:00:31.683 --> 00:00:35.517
Their brand identity combines Angkor motifs with modern design.

9
00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:39.141
Your turn. Say: Brand identity.

10
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.431
Brand identity.

11
00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:45.266
Brand equity.

12
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:50.026
Brand equity means the extra value a brand name adds to a product.

13
00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:53.731
Strong brand equity lets them charge 20% more.

14
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:56.725
Your turn. Say: Brand equity.

15
00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:00.858
Brand equity.

16
00:01:01.617 --> 00:01:02.873
Reputation.

17
00:01:03.883 --> 00:01:07.473
Reputation means the general opinion people hold about a company.

18
00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:11.186
One viral complaint damaged the hotel's reputation.

19
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:14.877
Your turn. Say: Reputation.

20
00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:18.909
Reputation.

21
00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.953
Brand loyalty.

22
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:25.912
Brand loyalty means customers' commitment to repeatedly buy one brand.

23
00:01:26.517 --> 00:01:29.491
Brand loyalty is high among older beer drinkers.

24
00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:33.061
Your turn. Say: Brand loyalty.

25
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.516
Brand loyalty.

26
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.541
Positioning statement.

27
00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:45.766
Positioning statement means a short description of a brand's target, benefit and difference.

28
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.441
The positioning statement guided every advertisement.

29
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.341
Your turn. Say: Positioning statement.

30
00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.665
Positioning statement.

31
00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.778
Visual identity.

32
00:02:00.783 --> 00:02:05.024
Visual identity means a brand's logo, colours, fonts and imagery.

33
00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:09.543
A consistent visual identity makes the brand instantly recognisable.

34
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:13.696
Your turn. Say: Visual identity.

35
00:02:16.533 --> 00:02:17.976
Visual identity.

36
00:02:18.717 --> 00:02:19.927
Brand voice.

37
00:02:20.917 --> 00:02:25.041
Brand voice means the personality and tone a brand uses in communication.

38
00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.253
Their brand voice is friendly but never childish.

39
00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.758
Your turn. Say: Brand voice.

40
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.949
Brand voice.

41
00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:37.708
Perception.

42
00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:41.900
Perception means the way something is understood or regarded.

43
00:02:42.517 --> 00:02:45.468
Customer perception improved after the redesign.

44
00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:48.527
Your turn. Say: Perception.

45
00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:52.472
Perception.

46
00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:56.720
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:57.583 --> 00:03:04.253
Visal, the bank changed its logo, colours and slogan three times in five years. Customers seem confused.

48
00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:15.932
That's the problem. A strong brand remains consistent across every channel, so people recognise it instantly and know what to expect.

49
00:03:17.017 --> 00:03:19.376
But brands need to stay modern, don't they?

50
00:03:20.483 --> 00:03:27.513
They do, gradually. The best brands consistently refresh details while their core promise remains the same.

51
00:03:28.617 --> 00:03:29.792
What should the bank do now?

52
00:03:30.883 --> 00:03:40.490
Choose one positioning statement and stick to it. Staff, adverts and the app should all consistently express the same values.

53
00:03:41.633 --> 00:03:43.192
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:47.884
Grammar focus: Consistency language (consistently, remains).

55
00:03:48.184 --> 00:03:49.440
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:53.357
A strong brand remains consistent across every channel.

57
00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.654
The best brands consistently deliver the same experience.

58
00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.235
The core promise stays unchanged for decades.

59
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:11.946
'Remain' and 'stay' are linking verbs, so they take an adjective (remains consistent), not an adverb. Use the adverb 'consistently' before an action verb (consistently delivers).

60
00:04:12.683 --> 00:04:16.555
Be careful! Don't say: The brand remains consistently.

61
00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.709
Say: The brand remains consistent.

62
00:04:21.009 --> 00:04:22.660
Remain + adjective.

63
00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:26.247
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.754
The Power of Consistency.

65
00:04:29.054 --> 00:04:34.572
Brand management is the long-term work of shaping how customers perceive a company and its products.

66
00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:41.723
Research consistently shows that people trust brands they recognise, and recognition depends on repetition.

67
00:04:42.733 --> 00:04:50.015
A brand whose visual identity and voice remain stable becomes a mental shortcut, saving customers the effort of comparing alternatives.

68
00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:57.678
However, consistency does not mean stagnation; successful brands update their style while their core promise remains intact.

69
00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:05.600
In the age of social media, every employee and every customer interaction either strengthens or weakens that promise.

70
00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.644
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:11.483 --> 00:05:13.820
Their service remains blank every year.

72
00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.098
A, consistently. B, consistent. C, consistency.

73
00:05:21.633 --> 00:05:23.389
The answer is B: consistent.

74
00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.757
A brand's logo, colours and fonts form its blank.

75
00:05:28.057 --> 00:05:32.314
A, visual identity. B, brand loyalty. C, reputation.

76
00:05:35.867 --> 00:05:38.168
The answer is A: visual identity.

77
00:05:39.317 --> 00:05:43.209
The personality and tone a brand uses in communication is its blank.

78
00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:47.452
A, perception. B, brand equity. C, brand voice.

79
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.534
The answer is C: brand voice.

80
00:05:54.683 --> 00:05:56.404
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:56.704 --> 00:06:06.105
A, The brand consistently delivers quality.. B, The brand delivers consistent quality always consistently.. C, The brand remains consistently strong quality..

82
00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:13.303
The answer is A: The brand consistently delivers quality..

83
00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:18.307
According to the reading, successful brands update their style while…

84
00:06:18.607 --> 00:06:24.617
A, changing their promise. B, their core promise remains intact. C, ignoring social media.

85
00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:31.594
The answer is B: their core promise remains intact.

86
00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.068
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:36.917 --> 00:06:40.112
What brand do you feel loyal to, and what builds that loyalty?

88
00:06:56.917 --> 00:06:58.545
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:58.845 --> 00:07:37.136
I feel loyal to a local bookshop chain because its experience remains consistent wherever I visit. The staff are always knowledgeable, the shops are calm and well organised, and the online store delivers exactly what it promises. What builds my loyalty is not advertising but reliability: I have never been disappointed. When prices are slightly higher than elsewhere, I still choose it because I trust it. In my view, loyalty grows from many small promises kept consistently over time.

90
00:07:37.436 --> 00:07:39.412
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:40.317 --> 00:07:45.871
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and consistency language (consistently, remains).

92
00:07:46.171 --> 00:07:50.856
Today's value is consistency. Keep your promises the same way, every day.

93
00:07:51.156 --> 00:07:53.843
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:54.143 --> 00:07:56.842
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

